  "question": {
    "text": "Twelve wires each having resistance $2 \\Omega$ are joined to form a cube. A battery of $6 \\mathrm{~V}$ emf is joined across point $a$ and $c$. The voltage difference between $e$ and $f$ is ______V.\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/pyHhpUz-LETgJCEdKvcCwwxvjzgSfvQJeIKapO253dg.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "1",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/GLYUgvMJndBFRP7jigwkuCsBdKJu0sgbzPRGrqeg0aE.original.fullsize.png\"><br />From symmetry, current through e-b & g-d =0\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\therefore \\mathrm{R}_{\\text {eq }}=\\frac{3}{4} \\times \\mathrm{R}=\\frac{3}{2} \\Omega \\\\\n& \\therefore \\text { Current through battery }=\\frac{6 \\times 2}{3}=4 \\mathrm{~A} \\\\\n& \\mathrm{i}_2=\\frac{4}{8} \\times 2=1 \\mathrm{~A} \\\\\n& \\therefore \\Delta \\mathrm{V} \\text { across e-f }=\\frac{\\mathrm{i}_2}{2} \\times \\mathrm{R}=\\frac{1}{2} \\times 2=1 \\mathrm{~V}\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
